.TH STORMBYTE-GITHUB 1 "August 2026" "StormByte" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
StormByte-GitHub \- helper script for managing StormByte GitHub repositories and submodules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B StormByte-GitHub
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B StormByte-GitHub
is a convenience wrapper around common Git and GitHub operations used in the StormByte project ecosystem.
It provides a consistent interface for cloning, updating, managing submodules and performing other
repository-related tasks across Linux, macOS and Windows (via Git Bash / MSYS2).

The script is designed to be quiet by default and only show detailed output when something fails
or when verbose mode is explicitly requested.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the general help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output (equivalent to setting BUILDMASTER_VERBOSE or similar debug flags).
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version of the script and exit.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS Repository management
.TP
.B clone \fI<repo>\fR [\fIdest\fR]
Clone a StormByte repository (shortcut for the full GitHub URL).
.TP
.B update [\fIrepo\fR...]
Fetch and pull the latest changes for the current repository or the specified ones.

.SS Submodules
.TP
.B submodules init
Initialize and update all submodules recursively
(\fBgit submodule update --init --recursive\fR).
This is the recommended first step after cloning a repository that uses submodules.
.TP
.B submodules update
Update already initialized submodules to the commits recorded in the superproject.
.TP
.B submodules status
Show the status of all submodules.

.SS Other
.TP
.B help [\fIcommand\fR]
Show help for a specific command (or the general help if no command is given).

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Clone a repository
StormByte-GitHub clone StormByte/BuildMaster

# Initialize submodules after cloning
cd BuildMaster
StormByte-GitHub submodules init

# Update everything
StormByte-GitHub update
StormByte-GitHub submodules update
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error (invalid arguments, git failure, etc.)
.TP
.B 2
Missing required tools (git, etc.)

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STORMBYTE_GITHUB_VERBOSE
If set to a non-empty value, enables verbose output (same as \fB\-\-verbose\fR).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/StormByte/GitHub.conf
Optional configuration file (future use).

.SH NOTES
- The script is intended to be used from the root of a StormByte repository or from anywhere when using the
  \fBclone\fR command.
- Submodule operations are recursive by default when using \fBsubmodules init\fR.
- On Windows the script expects a POSIX-compatible shell (Git Bash, MSYS2, WSL, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-submodule (1)

